## Section 2 — Secrets and Credentials

### F-001 — Dev-Only / Informational: `.env` files contain development credentials

**SEVERITY:** Informational (Dev Only)
**FILE:** `server/.env`, `client/.env`

> [!NOTE]
> **These are development-only values.** Git history scan ne confirm kiya ke yeh files kabhi commit nahi hui. Production deploy ke time real secrets ko environment variables (Render dashboard, Vercel dashboard) mein set karo — source code ya `.env` files mein nahi.

**Masla (Problem):** Agar kabhi bhi `.env` file accidentally commit ho jaye, to saray API keys public ho jayenge.

**Anjam (Consequences if not addressed before production):**
- Database access — koi bhi production DB read/write kar sakta hai
- AWS keys — attacker Lambda functions run kar ke aapka bill lakh rupay tak le ja sakta hai
- Stripe key — fake payments ya refunds generate ho sakte hain
- Claude API key — aapka AI quota exhaust ho jata hai, cost aati hai

**Fix — Production ke liye:**
```bash
# .env kabhi bhi commit mat karo
# Production secrets sirf deployment platform ke env vars mein dalo:
# Render Dashboard → Environment → Add Environment Variable
```

**Root `.gitignore` guard (ensure karo):**
```gitignore
# Root .gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
```

