## Section 4 — Authentication and Session Security

### F-006 — High: JWT Token URL Mein Leak Ho Raha Hai (Google OAuth Callback)

**SEVERITY:** High
**FILE:** `server/src/modules/auth/auth.controller.ts`
**LINE:** 115-118

**Masla (Roman Urdu):**
Google login ke baad user ko redirect kiya jata hai lekin JWT token URL ke andar `?token=...` ke saath laga diya jata hai. Yeh bahut badi security galti hai kyunke:
- Browser history mein token save ho jata hai
- Server access logs mein token likhta hai
- Agar callback page pe koi third-party script ho (Google Analytics, etc.) to unhe `Referer` header se token mil jata hai

**Anjam (Consequences):**
- Koi bhi jo browser history dekh sake (shared computer, malware) woh token le kar login kar sakta hai
- Server logs access karne wala bhi token steal kar sakta hai
- Token valid rahta hai puri JWT expiry tak (7 din)

**Current (Vulnerable — lines 115-118):**
```ts
let redirectUrl = `${frontendUrl}/auth/callback?success=true`;
if (isProduction && 'token' in authData && authData.token) {
  // Token URL mein daal diya — YAHI MASLA HAI
  redirectUrl = `${frontendUrl}/auth/callback?success=true&token=${encodeURIComponent(authData.token)}`;
}
return res.redirect(redirectUrl);
```

**Fix — Token URL se hatao. Cookie pehle se set ho chuki hai `generateTokenAndSetCookie()` mein:**
```ts
// auth.controller.ts — lines 115-120 replace karo:
const redirectUrl = `${frontendUrl}/auth/callback?success=true`;
return res.redirect(redirectUrl);
```

**`auth.service.ts` mein bhi token response se hatao (lines 238-250):**
```ts
// BEFORE (Problematic):
return {
  userId, email: user.email, fullName: user.fullName,
  role: user.role, planType: user.planType,
  ...(isProduction && { token }),  // <- YEH LINE HATAO
};

// AFTER (Fixed):
